# ============================================================
#  Controlled vocabularies (design §3.1). Character traits and
#  interests, roles, tones and memory kinds must come from these
#  lists; lint rejects anything else. Add a value here first.
# ============================================================

@vocab traits
desc: Personality traits for characters and archetypes.
values: proud ambitious lonely kind gentle homesick dreamy distant perceptive charming reckless loyal secretive chaotic curious stubborn guarded cold protective bold nosy idealistic overworked insecure bullying severe exacting dry warm eccentric patient calm watchful formidable fierce wary funny anxious honest sly brave shy

@vocab interests
desc: Things characters care about; used by casting and briefs.
values: duelling fire tides plants animals cooking prophecy painting tarot maps locks cards machines clocks flying stars snow writing gossip justice rules chess roses bees soup history teaching books music dancing money theatre

@vocab roles
desc: A character's place in the academy.
values: student prefect professor staff headmistress outsider villager

@vocab seeks
desc: How readily a character comes looking for you (design §5.5): often (the default; friends and rivals), sometimes, rarely (only once you've sought them out), never.
values: often sometimes rarely never

@vocab tones
desc: The mood of an event (design §5.2 variety, §12 `tone:`).
values: light warm tense grim eerie

@vocab memory_kinds
desc: What an option can leave behind in a character's memory (design §10.2).
values: helped hurt laughed fought confided kissed betrayed rescued protected abandoned

@vocab regions
desc: Where a place is (design §6.1). Internship hosts use internship:<host>.
values: castle grounds village wilds home travel internship

@vocab slots
desc: The parts of a day (design §4.2).
values: morning noon afternoon evening night midnight

@vocab houses
desc: Student houses.
values: Emberhall Rootward Stillwater Duskgate Brasswick Faculty

@vocab canon_allowlist
desc: Proper nouns that canon lint accepts without a worldbook entry: book and essay titles, potion names, headlines and other small props. Anything that matters to the world belongs in @lore instead.
values: Advanced Arcane Theory, Arcane, Curses of the Northern Wastes, Draught of Mild Courage, Draught of Unending Hiccups, Sleeping Draught, Magic and Duty, Nature of Absence, Potions, Pie-rates, Strike Again, Third Law of Correspondence, Brilliant Lectures, Brilliant Lecturers, Foundations of Flame
